The company is designing a privacy-forward home security camera that will "use AI to monitor the surrounding environment instead of actual video footage." It will apparently work with a new home security and monitoring service, but no additional detail on the service is included.<br/>
<br/>
Apple is planning to release a home hub for controlling smart home devices before the end of the year, and rumors have previously suggested there's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/11/11/kuo-apple-smart-home-camera-and-more-2026/">a camera in the works</a> to go along with it. Early rumors indicated it would be a wireless camera with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> integration and a connection <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/12/04/apple-smart-home-camera-rumor/">to the home hub</a> that's in development.<br/>
<br/>
Apple already has <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/homekit-secure-video/">HomeKit Secure Video</a>, an Apple Home feature for third-party cameras. &zwnj;HomeKit Secure Video&zwnj; features end-to-end encryption and uses <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/icloud/">iCloud</a> to securely stream and store video from compatible <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/homekit/">HomeKit</a> cameras.<br/>
<br/>
